From ed123b7c072be30df6b91e466794f2beef3dbc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:37:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Qt client: light the tiles the focus unit can reach this turn

With the Freeciv45 panels on, the tiles the head focus unit reaches with
the moves it has left are drawn on the map: a faint fill, so terrain and
resources show through, and a line along the range's outer edge. The
tiles come from the client goto's own path finding (terrain, zones of
control, borders, the tiles the player knows), through a new exported
fill_move_range_parameter(). A tile reached on the last move point
counts to path finding as next turn with full moves, so the moves spent
decide, not the turn. Unknown tiles stay black.

The range is worked out again when the unit, its tile, its moves or the
turn change, and every two seconds for other players' moves, from the
map's 200 ms timer. It clears with no focus unit, once the turn is done,
for another player's unit and while the city overlay is open.

A left click on the focus unit's own tile while an order is being given
(goto and the other hover modes) cancels it, goto line and all, and the
unit stays selected with no order. With no order, the click hides or
shows the range in place of the stack's selection popup; the unit bar's
chips select tile mates. A click there on an own city still opens it.

Issue 232.
